                    "rust_syntax": "mod name; pub use name::Type;",
                    "why_reserved": "Module trees define a crate's public surface — that is a LIBRARY concern. bare-bone doesn't know what its public surface looks like yet. Modules require knowing what you're exposing, which requires knowing your form. Premature module declarations create coupling before understanding.",
                    "promoted_by": ["library", "executable", "demo-test"],
                    "promotion_signal": "You need to organize code into submodules or re-export types from submodules"
