                            "Functions that compute derived values from identity — keep accessors pure (read-only)",
                            "Any function not related to PRAGMA/METADATA access — other functions go in CoreLogic or FreeFunctions",
                            "Caching or memoization — the statics are already compile-time; nothing to cache",
                            "Error handling — these functions cannot fail (the statics always exist)"
                        ],
                        "bare_bone_pattern": "4 commented-out functions: pragma(), pragma_get(), metadata(), metadata_get(). Implementation is IDENTICAL across all forms — copy exactly, uncomment. Only the doc comment examples change (file-specific keys).",
                        "why_these_constraints": "IdentityAccess is the bridge between compile-time identity (PRAGMA/METADATA statics in METADATA block) and runtime code that needs to read it. Every OmniCode file exposes these EXACT 4 functions. They are universal, immutable, and trivial — but they MUST exist because they ARE the runtime identity API."
                    }
