                    "status": "ACTIVE",
                    "purpose": "Primary operations — the actual work this file does",
                    "why_active": "Every file DOES something. CoreLogic is where that something lives. In bare-bone, this is minimal — skeleton implementations, placeholder logic. But the SECTION exists because the file will have logic.",
                    "bare_bone_content": "Skeleton impl blocks for CoreTypes defined in SETUP S7. Method signatures with todo!() bodies. Ready to fill.",
                    "content_constraints": {
                        "can_contain": [
                            "impl {TypeName} { ... } — method implementations on SETUP S7 types",
                            "pub fn method(&self, ...) -> ... — read operations",
                            "pub fn method(&mut self, ...) -> Result<(), Error> — mutation operations returning SETUP S6 error type",
                            "fn helper(&self, ...) -> ... — private helper methods (near the pub fns that call them)",
