                        ],
                        "bare_bone_pattern": "Commented-out impl block on the skeleton type from S7. Shows pub fn for primary operation, pub fn for state transformation (returns Result), fn for private helper. Each with doc comments and placeholder bodies. Derived files uncomment, fill with real logic.",
                        "why_these_constraints": "CoreLogic is the VERBS of the system — what the file actually DOES. It operates exclusively on types declared in SETUP. The impl block pattern keeps logic attached to its data. Private helpers live near the public functions that call them for readability. bare-bone provides the structural pattern; derived files fill in domain logic."
                    }
                },

                "B_FreeFunctions": {
                    "tag": "FreeFunctions",
                    "status": "ACTIVE",
                    "rust_syntax": "pub fn function_name(args) -> ReturnType { ... }",
                    "purpose": "Module-level public functions not attached to any type",
                    "why_active": "Every file may need standalone functions — convenience wrappers, register_identity(), utility operations. FreeFunctions is where they live. In bare-bone, this typically holds register_identity() for the identity system.",
                    "bare_bone_content": "register_identity() if this is an L0 crate. Minimal standalone functions.",
                    "content_constraints": {
                        "can_contain": [
