                            "One-shot utility functions that don't belong to any specific type",
                            "/// doc comments on every public function",
                            "In bare-bone: COMMENTED OUT — register_identity() skeleton showing the pattern"
                        ],
                        "cannot_contain": [
                            "Methods that should be on a type — if it takes &self or &mut self, it's an impl method, not free",
                            "main() or entry points — those belong in CLOSING Ce",
                            "Test functions — those belong in CLOSING Cv",
                            "Functions that duplicate type methods — use the type's API, don't wrap it unnecessarily",
                            "Internal helper functions for type methods — those go in CoreLogic impl blocks"
                        ],
                        "bare_bone_pattern": "Commented-out register_identity() function: calls bereshit_l0_identity::register() with the file's key, PRAGMA, and METADATA. Derived files uncomment if they're L0 crates; add domain-specific free functions.",
                        "why_these_constraints": "FreeFunctions are the top-level API — module-level functions not attached to any type. They exist for operations that span types or don't naturally belong to one type. register_identity() is the canonical example: it bridges THIS file's identity to the L0 registry system. bare-bone provides the registration pattern; derived files add domain-specific utilities."
                    }
                },

                "Reserved_Omission": {
                    "position": "LAST in BODY (after all active subsections)",
                    "status": "STRUCTURAL — required container",
                    "purpose": "Lists all BODY sections NOT active in this file. Completeness varies by form.",
                    "why_required": "BODY sections vary by form (library has 7, executable has 3, demo-test has 9). Reserved Omission lists everything this bare-bone file COULD become. It is the roadmap of potential.",
                    "bare_bone_content": [
